@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+---
+decision_id: cd-1-dbt-io
+status: accepted
+question: How does dbt read the lake, and how are marts published and refreshed
+choice: Dbt reads the lake through external read_parquet sources declared in sources.yml. Marts publish with materialized external to out/marts/<mart>/<mart>.parquet. The incremental stream mart (mart_edit_windows_5min) cannot be external, so it is materialized incremental with delete+insert on (wiki, namespace, actor_type, window_start). A post-hook writes out/marts/mart_edit_windows_5min/mart_edit_windows_5min.parquet after each run and replaces the previous file. The incremental filter recomputes every window that a new commit touches, using the last_commit_seq column.
+rationale: External reads keep the lake as the single source and need no load step in dbt. Recomputing touched windows makes the incremental result equal a full refresh, which a late event would otherwise break. The option rejected is a row-append incremental, which cannot correct a window after a late commit.
